    {
      "id": "p0247-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The translator paralleled this emotional change in Japanese by easing up on the disrespectful speech patterns. As part of this, Asriel eventually switches his personal pronoun to boku, which conveys a more innocent image befitting a scared young boy.",
        "raw": "The translator paralleled this emotional change in Japanese by easing up on\nthe disrespectful speech patterns. As part of this, Asriel eventually switches his\npersonal pronoun to boku, which conveys a more innocent image befitting a\nscared young boy.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09859836,
          0.52853571,
          0.70476074,
          0.59596429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09381193,
          0.52782143,
          0.70678889,
          0.59703571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          21,
          22,
          23,
          24
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "译者也在日文中逐步缓和无礼的语气，呼应这种情感变化。Asriel 最后改用 boku（我）自称，呈现出更天真、符合受惊小男孩的形象。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 42,
            "italic": true,
